    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474 2  General dishonesty with respect to a carriage service provider",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.17",
      "values:originalText": "Obtaining a gain\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if the person does anything with\nthe intention of dishonestly obtaining a gain from a carriage service\nprovider by way of the supply of a carriage service.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\nCausing a loss\n\n(2) A person is guilty of an offence if the person does anything with\nthe intention of dishonestly causing a loss to a carriage service\nprovider in connection with the supply of a carriage service.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(3) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person dishonestly causes a loss, or dishonestly causes a\nrisk of loss, to a carriage service provider in connection with\nthe supply of a carriage service; and\n\n(b) the person knows or believes that the loss will occur or that\nthere is a substantial risk of the loss occurring.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1",
      "skos:definition": "Obtaining a gain\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if the person does anything with\nthe intention of dishonestly obtaining a gain from a carriage service\nprovider by way of the supply of a carriage service.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\nCausing a loss\n\n(2) A person is guilty of an offence if the person does anything with\nthe intention of dishonestly causing a loss to a carriage service\nprovider in connection with the supply of a carriage service.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(3) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person dishonestly causes a loss, or dishonestly causes a\nrisk of loss, to a carriage service provider in connection with\nthe supply of a carriage service; and\n\n(b) the person knows or believes that the loss will occur or that\nthere is a substantial risk of the loss occurring.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-2-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "61e6dcfc4a09affe6e87a7df753c3d4bf4787c0bfacbb597989fb0c811bc69cb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "474 2  General dishonesty with respect to a carriage service provider",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 17,
      "values:originalText": "Obtaining a gain\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if the person does anything with\nthe intention of dishonestly obtaining a gain from a carriage service\nprovider by way of the supply of a carriage service.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\nCausing a loss\n\n(2) A person is guilty of an offence if the person does anything with\nthe intention of dishonestly causing a loss to a carriage service\nprovider in connection with the supply of a carriage service.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(3) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person dishonestly causes a loss, or dishonestly causes a\nrisk of loss, to a carriage service provider in connection with\nthe supply of a carriage service; and\n\n(b) the person knows or believes that the loss will occur or that\nthere is a substantial risk of the loss occurring.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1"
    },
