      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person is acting for the carrier or carriage service provider.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person is liable for the action."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-3-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The key includes an Allen interval representing the temporal relationship between actions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The key includes a clause describing the doing of something for or on behalf of a carriage service provider.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The action overlaps with another action."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-3-ss-2-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Repeats",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The key includes an LTL operator representing the repetition of actions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The key includes a clause describing the operation by that person of a facility in connection with the doing of that thing.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The action repeats."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-3-ss-2-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Diffuses",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The key includes a diffusion operator representing the spreading of actions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The key includes a clause describing the operation by that person of a facility in connection with the doing of that thing.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The action diffuses."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-3-ss-2-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recognizes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The key includes a CogAI operator recognizing the acting person.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The key includes a clause describing the doing by that person of that thing.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The system recognizes the acting person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474 4  Interception devices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) manufactures; or\n\n(ii) advertises, displays or offers for sale; or\n\n(iii) sells; or\n\n(iv) possesses;\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    13\n\nan apparatus or device (whether in an assembled or\nunassembled form); and\n\n(b) the apparatus or device is an interception device.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(2) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the person possesses the interception device in the\ncourse of the person’s duties relating to the interception of\ncommunications that does not constitute a contravention of\nsubsection 7(1) of the Telecommunications (Interception) Act\n1979.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\n\n(3) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the applicable conduct mentioned in\nsubparagraphs (1)(a)(i) to (iv) is in circumstances specified in\nregulations made for the purposes of this subsection.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) manufactures; or\n\n(ii) advertises, displays or offers for sale; or\n\n(iii) sells; or\n\n(iv) possesses;\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    13\n\nan apparatus or device (whether in an assembled or\nunassembled form); and\n\n(b) the apparatus or device is an interception device.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(2) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the person possesses the interception device in the\ncourse of the person’s duties relating to the interception of\ncommunications that does not constitute a contravention of\nsubsection 7(1) of the Telecommunications (Interception) Act\n1979.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\n\n(3) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the applicable conduct mentioned in\nsubparagraphs (1)(a)(i) to (iv) is in circumstances specified in\nregulations made for the purposes of this subsection.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-4-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-4-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-4-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c40f52625aae65e86060cbb88ed0222cf9c1d4e0a13b725a7c73671e2754708d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "474 4  Interception devices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) manufactures; or\n\n(ii) advertises, displays or offers for sale; or\n\n(iii) sells; or\n\n(iv) possesses;\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    13\n\nan apparatus or device (whether in an assembled or\nunassembled form); and\n\n(b) the apparatus or device is an interception device.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(2) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the person possesses the interception device in the\ncourse of the person’s duties relating to the interception of\ncommunications that does not constitute a contravention of\nsubsection 7(1) of the Telecommunications (Interception) Act\n1979.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\n\n(3) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the applicable conduct mentioned in\nsubparagraphs (1)(a)(i) to (iv) is in circumstances specified in\nregulations made for the purposes of this subsection.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3)."
    },
