    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474 5  Wrongful delivery of communications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) a communication is in the course of telecommunications\ncarriage; and\n\n(b) the person causes the communication to be received by a\nperson or carriage service other than the person or service to\nwhom it is directed.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 1 year.\n\n(2) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the person engages in the conduct referred to in\nparagraph (1)(b) with the consent or authorisation of the person to\nwhom, or the person operating the carriage service to which, the\ncommunication is directed.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) a communication is in the course of telecommunications\ncarriage; and\n\n(b) the person causes the communication to be received by a\nperson or carriage service other than the person or service to\nwhom it is directed.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 1 year.\n\n(2) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the person engages in the conduct referred to in\nparagraph (1)(b) with the consent or authorisation of the person to\nwhom, or the person operating the carriage service to which, the\ncommunication is directed.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-5-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-5-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "39aba5fe8049f99c12eee4bc2c5d70fe9a1dfde2667ded3f8c5ca7f9abd76ee0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "474 5  Wrongful delivery of communications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 19,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) a communication is in the course of telecommunications\ncarriage; and\n\n(b) the person causes the communication to be received by a\nperson or carriage service other than the person or service to\nwhom it is directed.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 1 year.\n\n(2) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the person engages in the conduct referred to in\nparagraph (1)(b) with the consent or authorisation of the person to\nwhom, or the person operating the carriage service to which, the\ncommunication is directed.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1"
    },
