    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-6-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474(7) 6  Interference with facilities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-6-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(7) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (5) if:\n\n(a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement\nofficer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in good\nfaith in the course of his or her duties; and\n\n(b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances\nfor the purpose of performing that duty.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\nNote 2:\nSee also subsection 475.1(2) for the interaction between this defence\nand the Radiocommunications Act 1992.",
      "skos:definition": "(7) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (5) if:\n\n(a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement\nofficer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in good\nfaith in the course of his or her duties; and\n\n(b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances\nfor the purpose of performing that duty.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\nNote 2:\nSee also subsection 475.1(2) for the interaction between this defence\nand the Radiocommunications Act 1992.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-6"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-6-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-6-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f974497d00d409f0a13e96586458aff00517dd88df505a4953518043fc0f134b",
      "skos:note": "Defendant bears evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-6-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "474(7) 6  Interference with facilities",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "(7) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (5) if:\n\n(a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement\nofficer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in good\nfaith in the course of his or her duties; and\n\n(b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances\nfor the purpose of performing that duty.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\nNote 2:\nSee also subsection 475.1(2) for the interaction between this defence\nand the Radiocommunications Act 1992."
    },
