    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-8-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474(4) Section 474",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-8-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the person is:\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    17\n\n(a) the manufacturer of the mobile telecommunications device in\nwhich the telecommunications device identifier is installed;\nor\n\n(b) an employee or agent of the manufacturer who is acting on\nbehalf of the manufacturer; or\n\n(c) acting with the consent of the manufacturer.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the person is:\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    17\n\n(a) the manufacturer of the mobile telecommunications device in\nwhich the telecommunications device identifier is installed;\nor\n\n(b) an employee or agent of the manufacturer who is acting on\nbehalf of the manufacturer; or\n\n(c) acting with the consent of the manufacturer.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-8"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-8-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-8-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1300c75bbdfff08d9136d73dcba662dad6a59c8c024c089b490e6a5759613725",
      "skos:note": "Defendant bears evidential burden in relation to the matter."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-8-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "474(4) Section 474",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the person is:\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    17\n\n(a) the manufacturer of the mobile telecommunications device in\nwhich the telecommunications device identifier is installed;\nor\n\n(b) an employee or agent of the manufacturer who is acting on\nbehalf of the manufacturer; or\n\n(c) acting with the consent of the manufacturer.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3)."
    },
