    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-8-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474(5) Section 474",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-8-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(5) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if:\n\n(a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement\nofficer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in the\ncourse of his or her duties; and\n\n(b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances\nfor the purpose of performing that duty.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\nNote 2:\nThis subsection merely creates a defence to an offence against\nsubsection (1) and does not operate to authorise any conduct that\nrequires a warrant under some other law.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if:\n\n(a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement\nofficer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in the\ncourse of his or her duties; and\n\n(b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances\nfor the purpose of performing that duty.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\nNote 2:\nThis subsection merely creates a defence to an offence against\nsubsection (1) and does not operate to authorise any conduct that\nrequires a warrant under some other law.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-8"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-8-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-8-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "74958a2c0c44e1c87d156f6cb258b001cd771b7e0ee25c94ac7a060bcd4dfef8",
      "skos:note": "Defence to criminal responsibility for law enforcement or intelligence officers acting in duty"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-8-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "474(5) Section 474",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(5) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if:\n\n(a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement\nofficer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in the\ncourse of his or her duties; and\n\n(b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances\nfor the purpose of performing that duty.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\nNote 2:\nThis subsection merely creates a defence to an offence against\nsubsection (1) and does not operate to authorise any conduct that\nrequires a warrant under some other law."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-8-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-8-ss-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-8-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defence to criminal responsibility",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Acting in duty",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Not criminally responsible"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474 9  Producing, supplying or obtaining data or a device with intent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "to modify a telecommunications device identifier\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person produces, supplies or obtains any thing or data;\nand\n\n(b) the person does so with the intention that the thing or data be\nused:\n\n(i) by the person; or\n\n(ii) by another person;\n\nin committing an offence against subsection 474.7(1)\n(modification of a telecommunications device identifier).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)\neven if committing the offence against subsection 474.7(1)\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1",
      "skos:definition": "to modify a telecommunications device identifier\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person produces, supplies or obtains any thing or data;\nand\n\n(b) the person does so with the intention that the thing or data be\nused:\n\n(i) by the person; or\n\n(ii) by another person;\n\nin committing an offence against subsection 474.7(1)\n(modification of a telecommunications device identifier).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)\neven if committing the offence against subsection 474.7(1)\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-9-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-9-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0ee5e208f22655dc2e236d9d9f91159d97d1b06d9bd413c77b91dd2fa3d8d696"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "474 9  Producing, supplying or obtaining data or a device with intent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "to modify a telecommunications device identifier\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person produces, supplies or obtains any thing or data;\nand\n\n(b) the person does so with the intention that the thing or data be\nused:\n\n(i) by the person; or\n\n(ii) by another person;\n\nin committing an offence against subsection 474.7(1)\n(modification of a telecommunications device identifier).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)\neven if committing the offence against subsection 474.7(1)\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1"
    },
