      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if the person:\n\n(a) copies the subscription-specific secure data from an account\nidentifier; and\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    19\n\n(b) does so with the intention that the data will be copied\n(whether by the person or by someone else) onto something\nthat:\n\n(i) is an account identifier; or\n\n(ii) will, once the data is copied onto it, be capable of\noperating as an account identifier.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\nCopying subscription-specific secure data onto a new account\nidentifier",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if the person:\n\n(a) copies the subscription-specific secure data from an account\nidentifier; and\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    19\n\n(b) does so with the intention that the data will be copied\n(whether by the person or by someone else) onto something\nthat:\n\n(i) is an account identifier; or\n\n(ii) will, once the data is copied onto it, be capable of\noperating as an account identifier.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\nCopying subscription-specific secure data onto a new account\nidentifier",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-10"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
