    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474 12  Producing, supplying or obtaining data or a device with",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "intent to copy an account identifier\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person produces, supplies or obtains any thing or data;\nand\n\n(b) the person does so with the intention that the thing or data be\nused:\n\n(i) by the person; or\n\n(ii) by another person;\n\nin committing an offence against subsection 474.10(1)\n(copying subscription-specific secure data from an account\nidentifier) or 474.10(2) (copying subscription-specific secure\ndata onto an account identifier).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1",
      "skos:definition": "intent to copy an account identifier\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person produces, supplies or obtains any thing or data;\nand\n\n(b) the person does so with the intention that the thing or data be\nused:\n\n(i) by the person; or\n\n(ii) by another person;\n\nin committing an offence against subsection 474.10(1)\n(copying subscription-specific secure data from an account\nidentifier) or 474.10(2) (copying subscription-specific secure\ndata onto an account identifier).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-12-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-12-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "62527805c639ccbee314cbd8bdc3c0b9bd0a94ca9344a34db2578468816d8358",
      "skos:note": "Producing, supplying or obtaining data with intent to copy an account identifier is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "474 12  Producing, supplying or obtaining data or a device with",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "intent to copy an account identifier\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person produces, supplies or obtains any thing or data;\nand\n\n(b) the person does so with the intention that the thing or data be\nused:\n\n(i) by the person; or\n\n(ii) by another person;\n\nin committing an offence against subsection 474.10(1)\n(copying subscription-specific secure data from an account\nidentifier) or 474.10(2) (copying subscription-specific secure\ndata onto an account identifier).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-12-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-12"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-12-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits producing, supplying or obtaining data with intent to copy an account identifier.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "22 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-22"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "Other Measures) Act (No. 2) 2004\n\n(2) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)\neven if committing the offence against subsection 474.10(1)\n(copying subscription-specific secure data from an account\nidentifier) or 474.10(2) (copying subscription-specific secure data\nonto an account identifier) is impossible.\n\n(3) It is not an offence to attempt to commit an offence against\nsubsection (1).\nDefences\n\n(4) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the person is:\n\n(a) the carrier who operates the facilities used, or to be used, in\nthe supply of the public mobile telecommunications service\nto which the subscription-specific secure data relates; or\n\n(b) an employee or agent of that carrier who is acting on behalf\nof that carrier; or\n\n(c) acting with the consent of that carrier.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\n\n(5) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if:\n\n(a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement\nofficer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in the\ncourse of his or her duties; and\n\n(b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances\nfor the purpose of performing that duty.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\nNote 2:\nThis subsection merely creates a defence to an offence against\nsubsection (1) and does not operate to authorise any conduct that\nrequires a warrant under some other law.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    23\nSubdivision C—Offences related to use of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "Other Measures) Act (No. 2) 2004\n\n(2) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)\neven if committing the offence against subsection 474.10(1)\n(copying subscription-specific secure data from an account\nidentifier) or 474.10(2) (copying subscription-specific secure data\nonto an account identifier) is impossible.\n\n(3) It is not an offence to attempt to commit an offence against\nsubsection (1).\nDefences\n\n(4) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the person is:\n\n(a) the carrier who operates the facilities used, or to be used, in\nthe supply of the public mobile telecommunications service\nto which the subscription-specific secure data relates; or\n\n(b) an employee or agent of that carrier who is acting on behalf\nof that carrier; or\n\n(c) acting with the consent of that carrier.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\n\n(5) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if:\n\n(a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement\nofficer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in the\ncourse of his or her duties; and\n\n(b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances\nfor the purpose of performing that duty.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\nNote 2:\nThis subsection merely creates a defence to an offence against\nsubsection (1) and does not operate to authorise any conduct that\nrequires a warrant under some other law.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    23\nSubdivision C—Offences related to use of telecommunications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "70719854dfa00c09ece83b775c3f4460984b1e899137f68516fb24a9be21d0fb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-22",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "Other Measures) Act (No. 2) 2004\n\n(2) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)\neven if committing the offence against subsection 474.10(1)\n(copying subscription-specific secure data from an account\nidentifier) or 474.10(2) (copying subscription-specific secure data\nonto an account identifier) is impossible.\n\n(3) It is not an offence to attempt to commit an offence against\nsubsection (1).\nDefences\n\n(4) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the person is:\n\n(a) the carrier who operates the facilities used, or to be used, in\nthe supply of the public mobile telecommunications service\nto which the subscription-specific secure data relates; or\n\n(b) an employee or agent of that carrier who is acting on behalf\nof that carrier; or\n\n(c) acting with the consent of that carrier.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\n\n(5) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if:\n\n(a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement\nofficer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in the\ncourse of his or her duties; and\n\n(b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances\nfor the purpose of performing that duty.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\nNote 2:\nThis subsection merely creates a defence to an offence against\nsubsection (1) and does not operate to authorise any conduct that\nrequires a warrant under some other law.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    23\nSubdivision C—Offences related to use of telecommunications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-2",
