    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "22(4) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-22-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the person is:\n\n(a) the carrier who operates the facilities used, or to be used, in\nthe supply of the public mobile telecommunications service\nto which the subscription-specific secure data relates; or\n\n(b) an employee or agent of that carrier who is acting on behalf\nof that carrier; or\n\n(c) acting with the consent of that carrier.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the person is:\n\n(a) the carrier who operates the facilities used, or to be used, in\nthe supply of the public mobile telecommunications service\nto which the subscription-specific secure data relates; or\n\n(b) an employee or agent of that carrier who is acting on behalf\nof that carrier; or\n\n(c) acting with the consent of that carrier.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-4-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-4-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e351b7d5b8755c579d2f34d95eb4439d89756e75cca7d12a009fc2a10dac1ddd",
      "skos:note": "A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against subsection (1) if the person is: ..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-22-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22(4) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if the person is:\n\n(a) the carrier who operates the facilities used, or to be used, in\nthe supply of the public mobile telecommunications service\nto which the subscription-specific secure data relates; or\n\n(b) an employee or agent of that carrier who is acting on behalf\nof that carrier; or\n\n(c) acting with the consent of that carrier.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
