      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "exemption",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Exemptions from criminal responsibility",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person is the carrier who operates the facilities used, or to be used, in the supply of the public mobile telecommunications service",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person is not criminally responsible for an offence against subsection (1)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-4-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "permission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission from the carrier to act",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person is acting with the consent of that carrier",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person is not criminally responsible for an offence against subsection (1)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "during",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal relationship between carrier and employee/agent",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person is an employee or agent of that carrier who is acting on behalf of that carrier",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The carrier's consent is required for the employee/agent to act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-4-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "exemption",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Exemptions from criminal responsibility based on role",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person is an employee or agent of that carrier who is acting on behalf of that carrier",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person is not criminally responsible for an offence against subsection (1)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "22(5) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-22-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(5) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if:\n\n(a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement\nofficer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in the\ncourse of his or her duties; and\n\n(b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances\nfor the purpose of performing that duty.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\nNote 2:\nThis subsection merely creates a defence to an offence against\nsubsection (1) and does not operate to authorise any conduct that\nrequires a warrant under some other law.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    23\nSubdivision C—Offences related to use of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(5) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if:\n\n(a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement\nofficer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in the\ncourse of his or her duties; and\n\n(b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances\nfor the purpose of performing that duty.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\nNote 2:\nThis subsection merely creates a defence to an offence against\nsubsection (1) and does not operate to authorise any conduct that\nrequires a warrant under some other law.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    23\nSubdivision C—Offences related to use of telecommunications",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2b08080ae9ed029b919a9862019bd85f1a07192860575c63c801a0765efab81c",
      "skos:note": "Defence to criminal liability for law enforcement or intelligence officers acting in duty"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-22-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22(5) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(5) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against\nsubsection (1) if:\n\n(a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement\nofficer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in the\ncourse of his or her duties; and\n\n(b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances\nfor the purpose of performing that duty.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection, see subsection 13.3(3).\nNote 2:\nThis subsection merely creates a defence to an offence against\nsubsection (1) and does not operate to authorise any conduct that\nrequires a warrant under some other law.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    23\nSubdivision C—Offences related to use of telecommunications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-22-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defence to criminal liability",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Law enforcement or intelligence officer acting in duty",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Not criminally responsible"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-13",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474 13  Use of a carriage service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-13"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Subdivision, a person is taken not to use a\ncarriage service by engaging in particular conduct if:\n\n(a) the person is a carrier and, in engaging in that conduct, is\nacting solely in the person’s capacity as a carrier; or\n\n(b) the person is a carriage service provider and, in engaging in\nthat conduct, is acting solely in the person’s capacity as a\ncarriage service provider; or\n\n(c) the person is an Internet service provider and, in engaging in\nthat conduct, is acting solely in the person’s capacity as an\nInternet service provider; or\n\n(d) the person is an Internet content host and, in engaging in that\nconduct, is acting solely in the person’s capacity as an\nInternet content host.",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of this Subdivision, a person is taken not to use a\ncarriage service by engaging in particular conduct if:\n\n(a) the person is a carrier and, in engaging in that conduct, is\nacting solely in the person’s capacity as a carrier; or\n\n(b) the person is a carriage service provider and, in engaging in\nthat conduct, is acting solely in the person’s capacity as a\ncarriage service provider; or\n\n(c) the person is an Internet service provider and, in engaging in\nthat conduct, is acting solely in the person’s capacity as an\nInternet service provider; or\n\n(d) the person is an Internet content host and, in engaging in that\nconduct, is acting solely in the person’s capacity as an\nInternet content host.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-13-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-13-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-13-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-13-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-13-logic-cogai-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-13-logic-shacl-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "649bb6b17b1847531cb1d771e6c03b973b502908bbe907be80ac187a779d3f7e",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions from using a carriage service"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-13",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "474 13  Use of a carriage service",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Subdivision, a person is taken not to use a\ncarriage service by engaging in particular conduct if:\n\n(a) the person is a carrier and, in engaging in that conduct, is\nacting solely in the person’s capacity as a carrier; or\n\n(b) the person is a carriage service provider and, in engaging in\nthat conduct, is acting solely in the person’s capacity as a\ncarriage service provider; or\n\n(c) the person is an Internet service provider and, in engaging in\nthat conduct, is acting solely in the person’s capacity as an\nInternet service provider; or\n\n(d) the person is an Internet content host and, in engaging in that\nconduct, is acting solely in the person’s capacity as an\nInternet content host."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-13-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-13"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-13-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "exemption",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Exemptions from using a carriage service",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person is acting solely in their capacity as a carrier/service provider/internet content host",
      "cml:conclusionText": "No obligation to use a carriage service"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-13-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "during",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal relationship between exemption and obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person is exempt from using a carriage service during their capacity as a carrier/service provider/internet content host",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Exemption occurs during the person's capacity"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-13-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "until",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal relationship between exemption and obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person is exempt from using a carriage service until their capacity as a carrier/service provider/internet content host ends",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Exemption occurs until the person's capacity ends"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-13-logic-cogai-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "isA",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Classification of exemption as a type of obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The exemption is a type of obligation to not use a carriage service",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Exemption is a subclass of the obligation to not use a carriage service"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-13-logic-shacl-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:SHACL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "asserts",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Validation of exemption against a schema",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::shacl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The exemption asserts that the person is exempt from using a carriage service",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Exemption is validated against the schema"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-14",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474 14  Using a telecommunications network with intention to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-14"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "commit a serious offence\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) connects equipment to a telecommunications network;\nand\n\n(ii) intends by this to commit, or to facilitate the\ncommission of, an offence (whether by that person or\nanother person); and\n\n(b) the offence is:\n\n(i) a serious offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a\nState or a Territory; or\n\n(ii) a serious offence against a foreign law.\n\n(2) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person uses equipment connected to a\ntelecommunications network in the commission of, or to\nfacilitate the commission of, an offence (whether by that\nperson or another person); and\n\n(b) the offence is:\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1",
