    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-15",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474 15  Using a carriage service to make a threat",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-15"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "Threat to kill\n\n(1) A person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person uses a carriage service to make to another\nperson (the second person) a threat to kill the second person\nor a third person; and\n\n(b) the first person intends the second person to fear that the\nthreat will be carried out.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\nThreat to cause serious harm\n\n(2) A person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person uses a carriage service to make to another\nperson (the second person) a threat to cause serious harm to\nthe second person or a third person; and\n\n(b) the first person intends the second person to fear that the\nthreat will be carried out.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    25\nActual fear not necessary\n\n(3) In a prosecution for an offence against this section, it is not\nnecessary to prove that the person receiving the threat actually\nfeared that the threat would be carried out.\nDefinitions\n\n(4) In this section:\nfear includes apprehension.\nthreat to cause serious harm to a person includes a threat to\nsubstantially contribute to serious harm to the person.",
      "skos:definition": "Threat to kill\n\n(1) A person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person uses a carriage service to make to another\nperson (the second person) a threat to kill the second person\nor a third person; and\n\n(b) the first person intends the second person to fear that the\nthreat will be carried out.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\nThreat to cause serious harm\n\n(2) A person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person uses a carriage service to make to another\nperson (the second person) a threat to cause serious harm to\nthe second person or a third person; and\n\n(b) the first person intends the second person to fear that the\nthreat will be carried out.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    25\nActual fear not necessary\n\n(3) In a prosecution for an offence against this section, it is not\nnecessary to prove that the person receiving the threat actually\nfeared that the threat would be carried out.\nDefinitions\n\n(4) In this section:\nfear includes apprehension.\nthreat to cause serious harm to a person includes a threat to\nsubstantially contribute to serious harm to the person.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-15-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-15-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-15-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-15-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8d47fbbdf99b2d53e65455ab787e3475e6ef8d810092649935773bd956119d09"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-15",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "474 15  Using a carriage service to make a threat",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "Threat to kill\n\n(1) A person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person uses a carriage service to make to another\nperson (the second person) a threat to kill the second person\nor a third person; and\n\n(b) the first person intends the second person to fear that the\nthreat will be carried out.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\nThreat to cause serious harm\n\n(2) A person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person uses a carriage service to make to another\nperson (the second person) a threat to cause serious harm to\nthe second person or a third person; and\n\n(b) the first person intends the second person to fear that the\nthreat will be carried out.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    25\nActual fear not necessary\n\n(3) In a prosecution for an offence against this section, it is not\nnecessary to prove that the person receiving the threat actually\nfeared that the threat would be carried out.\nDefinitions\n\n(4) In this section:\nfear includes apprehension.\nthreat to cause serious harm to a person includes a threat to\nsubstantially contribute to serious harm to the person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-15-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474(1) 15  Using a carriage service to make a threat",
