      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person uses a carriage service to make to another\nperson (the second person) a threat to cause serious harm to\nthe second person or a third person; and\n\n(b) the first person intends the second person to fear that the\nthreat will be carried out.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    25\nActual fear not necessary",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person uses a carriage service to make to another\nperson (the second person) a threat to cause serious harm to\nthe second person or a third person; and\n\n(b) the first person intends the second person to fear that the\nthreat will be carried out.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    25\nActual fear not necessary",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-15"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-15-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-15-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ae9a73bdbee7c14230370c84470468ae2a62436e55af826f2e89763f18726b48",
      "skos:note": "Using a carriage service to make a threat is an offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-15-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "474(2) 15  Using a carriage service to make a threat",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person uses a carriage service to make to another\nperson (the second person) a threat to cause serious harm to\nthe second person or a third person; and\n\n(b) the first person intends the second person to fear that the\nthreat will be carried out.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years.\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    25\nActual fear not necessary"
    },
