        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person uses a carriage service to send a communication.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The act is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-16-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes a duty on the person to not use a carriage service for a hoax threat.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person must not use a carriage service for a hoax threat."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-16-logic-linearlogic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implication",
      "cml:logicSummary": "If the person uses a carriage service to send a communication, then they are guilty of an offence if...",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person does so with the intention of inducing a false belief...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The act implies guilt."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-16-logic-alleninterval-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Temporal relation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The use of a carriage service for a hoax threat occurs at the same time as the communication is sent.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person uses a carriage service to send a communication; and...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The act occurs simultaneously."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-16-logic-diffusion-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Spread",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The hoax threat spreads through the use of a carriage service.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person does so with the intention of inducing a false belief...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The act spreads."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-17",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474 17  Using a carriage service to menace, harass or cause offence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-17"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.31",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person uses a carriage service; and\n\n(b) the person does so in a way (whether by the method of use or\nthe content of a communication, or both) that reasonable\npersons would regard as being, in all the circumstances,\nmenacing, harassing or offensive.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 3 years.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), that subsection applies to\nmenacing, harassing or causing offence to:\n\n(a) an employee of the NRS provider; or\n\n(b) an emergency call person; or\n\n(c) an employee of an emergency service organisation; or\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person uses a carriage service; and\n\n(b) the person does so in a way (whether by the method of use or\nthe content of a communication, or both) that reasonable\npersons would regard as being, in all the circumstances,\nmenacing, harassing or offensive.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 3 years.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), that subsection applies to\nmenacing, harassing or causing offence to:\n\n(a) an employee of the NRS provider; or\n\n(b) an emergency call person; or\n\n(c) an employee of an emergency service organisation; or\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-17-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-17-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a02f74bc19bcd38c4570e80c3e76ebad52b7d30033db76d9173d1ebde0544e86"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "474 17  Using a carriage service to menace, harass or cause offence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 31,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person uses a carriage service; and\n\n(b) the person does so in a way (whether by the method of use or\nthe content of a communication, or both) that reasonable\npersons would regard as being, in all the circumstances,\nmenacing, harassing or offensive.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 3 years.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), that subsection applies to\nmenacing, harassing or causing offence to:\n\n(a) an employee of the NRS provider; or\n\n(b) an emergency call person; or\n\n(c) an employee of an emergency service organisation; or\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1"
    },
