      "cml:operator": "Implication",
      "cml:logicSummary": "If a person makes an emergency call for non-emergency purposes, then they are guilty of an offence.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Making an emergency call for non-emergency purposes implies guilt."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-2-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits imprisonment for 3 years as a penalty for making an emergency call for non-emergency purposes.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Imprisonment for 3 years is prohibited as a penalty for making an emergency call for non-emergency purposes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474(3) 18  Improper use of emergency call service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "(3) In determining whether a call by a person to an emergency service\nnumber is a vexatious one, have regard to:\n\n(a) the content of the call; and\n\n(b) the number, frequency and content of previous calls the\nperson has made to emergency service numbers otherwise\nthan for the purpose of reporting emergencies; and\n\n(c) any other relevant matter.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) In determining whether a call by a person to an emergency service\nnumber is a vexatious one, have regard to:\n\n(a) the content of the call; and\n\n(b) the number, frequency and content of previous calls the\nperson has made to emergency service numbers otherwise\nthan for the purpose of reporting emergencies; and\n\n(c) any other relevant matter.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "691f24b722d895f1e919b774645667d1aa46dae5a9d581b76437a6f0c4591d1e",
      "skos:note": "Determine whether a call is vexatious based on previous calls and content."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "474(3) 18  Improper use of emergency call service",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "(3) In determining whether a call by a person to an emergency service\nnumber is a vexatious one, have regard to:\n\n(a) the content of the call; and\n\n(b) the number, frequency and content of previous calls the\nperson has made to emergency service numbers otherwise\nthan for the purpose of reporting emergencies; and\n\n(c) any other relevant matter."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Duty to determine vexatious calls",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Call by person to emergency service number is a vexatious one.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "State must determine whether call is vexatious."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "between",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Consider time interval between calls",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Call by person to emergency service number has a previous call within a certain time interval.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "State must consider time interval between calls when determining vexatiousness."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "until",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Consider frequency of calls until it becomes vexatious",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Call by person to emergency service number has a certain frequency until it becomes vexatious.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "State must consider frequency of calls until it becomes vexatious when determining vexatiousness."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "through",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Consider content and previous calls diffused through state",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Call by person to emergency service number has content that is diffused through the state.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "State must consider content and previous calls diffused through the state when determining vexatiousness."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-18-ss-3-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "with",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Consider AI assistance in determining vexatious calls",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "State uses AI assistance to determine vexatious calls.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "State must consider AI assistance when determining vexatiousness."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-19",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474 19  Using a carriage service for child pornography material",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-19"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) uses a carriage service to access material; or\n\n(ii) uses a carriage service to cause material to be\ntransmitted to the person; or\n\n(iii) uses a carriage service to transmit material; or\n\n(iv) uses a carriage service to make material available; or\n\n(v) uses a carriage service to publish or otherwise distribute\nmaterial; and\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    27\n\n(b) the material is child pornography material.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, the following are the fault elements for the\nphysical elements of an offence against subsection (1):\n\n(a) intention is the fault element for the conduct referred to in\nparagraph (1)(a);\n\n(b) recklessness is the fault element for the circumstances\nreferred to in paragraph (1)(b).\nNote:\nFor the meaning of intention and recklessness see sections 5.2 and",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) uses a carriage service to access material; or\n\n(ii) uses a carriage service to cause material to be\ntransmitted to the person; or\n\n(iii) uses a carriage service to transmit material; or\n\n(iv) uses a carriage service to make material available; or\n\n(v) uses a carriage service to publish or otherwise distribute\nmaterial; and\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    27\n\n(b) the material is child pornography material.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, the following are the fault elements for the\nphysical elements of an offence against subsection (1):\n\n(a) intention is the fault element for the conduct referred to in\nparagraph (1)(a);\n\n(b) recklessness is the fault element for the circumstances\nreferred to in paragraph (1)(b).\nNote:\nFor the meaning of intention and recklessness see sections 5.2 and",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-19-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-19-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "175911c15338a4c565841d4bacc19a0f1e8b8f09d94d11bba66c15e9bedfcf7e"
    },
