    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-20",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474 20  Possessing, controlling, producing, supplying or obtaining",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-20"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "child pornography material for use through a carriage\nservice\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) has possession or control of material; or\n\n(ii) produces, supplies or obtains material; and\n\n(b) the material is child pornography material; and\n\n(c) the person has that possession or control, or engages in that\nproduction, supply or obtaining, with the intention that the\nmaterial be used:\n\n(i) by that person; or\n\n(ii) by another person;\n\nin committing an offence against section 474.19 (using a\ncarriage service for child pornography material).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(2) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)\neven if committing the offence against section 474.19 (using a\ncarriage service for child pornography material) is impossible.\n\n(3) It is not an offence to attempt to commit an offence against\nsubsection (1).\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1",
      "skos:definition": "child pornography material for use through a carriage\nservice\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) has possession or control of material; or\n\n(ii) produces, supplies or obtains material; and\n\n(b) the material is child pornography material; and\n\n(c) the person has that possession or control, or engages in that\nproduction, supply or obtaining, with the intention that the\nmaterial be used:\n\n(i) by that person; or\n\n(ii) by another person;\n\nin committing an offence against section 474.19 (using a\ncarriage service for child pornography material).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(2) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)\neven if committing the offence against section 474.19 (using a\ncarriage service for child pornography material) is impossible.\n\n(3) It is not an offence to attempt to commit an offence against\nsubsection (1).\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-20-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-20-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-20-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1ef1abcb8b50140f29af162819b12c302fb64168bd2798a3d0be258fddf80080"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-474-20",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "474 20  Possessing, controlling, producing, supplying or obtaining",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "child pornography material for use through a carriage\nservice\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) has possession or control of material; or\n\n(ii) produces, supplies or obtains material; and\n\n(b) the material is child pornography material; and\n\n(c) the person has that possession or control, or engages in that\nproduction, supply or obtaining, with the intention that the\nmaterial be used:\n\n(i) by that person; or\n\n(ii) by another person;\n\nin committing an offence against section 474.19 (using a\ncarriage service for child pornography material).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(2) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)\neven if committing the offence against section 474.19 (using a\ncarriage service for child pornography material) is impossible.\n\n(3) It is not an offence to attempt to commit an offence against\nsubsection (1).\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1"
    },
