      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.42",
      "values:originalText": "(9) For the purposes of sections 474.26 and 474.27, it does not matter\nthat the recipient to whom the sender believes the sender is\n\nTelecommunications offences  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    37\ntransmitting the communication is a fictitious person represented to\nthe sender as a real person.\nAttempt not offence",
