    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-475",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "475 1  Saving of other laws",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-475"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This Part is not intended to exclude or limit the operation of any\nother law of the Commonwealth or any law of a State or Territory.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), a provision in this Part to the\neffect that a person is not criminally responsible for an offence\nagainst a provision of this Part in relation to particular conduct\ndoes not make the conduct lawful if it would otherwise be unlawful\nunder the Radiocommunications Act 1992.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This Part is not intended to exclude or limit the operation of any\nother law of the Commonwealth or any law of a State or Territory.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), a provision in this Part to the\neffect that a person is not criminally responsible for an offence\nagainst a provision of this Part in relation to particular conduct\ndoes not make the conduct lawful if it would otherwise be unlawful\nunder the Radiocommunications Act 1992.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-475-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-475-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "294893b81716c5f1007c931c927a6cf5988f83d73f73b79bb4077396c79735ec"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-475",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "475 1  Saving of other laws",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This Part is not intended to exclude or limit the operation of any\nother law of the Commonwealth or any law of a State or Territory.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), a provision in this Part to the\neffect that a person is not criminally responsible for an offence\nagainst a provision of this Part in relation to particular conduct\ndoes not make the conduct lawful if it would otherwise be unlawful\nunder the Radiocommunications Act 1992."
    },
