    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-40",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-40"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "Other Measures) Act (No. 2) 2004\nActual fear not necessary\n\n(3) In a prosecution for an offence against this section, it is not\nnecessary to prove that the person receiving the threat actually\nfeared that the threat would be carried out.\nDefinitions\n\n(4) In this section:\nfear includes apprehension.\nthreat to cause serious harm to a person includes a threat to\nsubstantially contribute to serious harm to the person.",
      "skos:definition": "Other Measures) Act (No. 2) 2004\nActual fear not necessary\n\n(3) In a prosecution for an offence against this section, it is not\nnecessary to prove that the person receiving the threat actually\nfeared that the threat would be carried out.\nDefinitions\n\n(4) In this section:\nfear includes apprehension.\nthreat to cause serious harm to a person includes a threat to\nsubstantially contribute to serious harm to the person.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-40-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-40-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "33b421e7ab10951ffb5e869b0be3249d386dea500d9f5eba530a6a5b1a5835c2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-40",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "Other Measures) Act (No. 2) 2004\nActual fear not necessary\n\n(3) In a prosecution for an offence against this section, it is not\nnecessary to prove that the person receiving the threat actually\nfeared that the threat would be carried out.\nDefinitions\n\n(4) In this section:\nfear includes apprehension.\nthreat to cause serious harm to a person includes a threat to\nsubstantially contribute to serious harm to the person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-40-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40(3) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-40-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "(3) In a prosecution for an offence against this section, it is not\nnecessary to prove that the person receiving the threat actually\nfeared that the threat would be carried out.\nDefinitions",
      "skos:definition": "(3) In a prosecution for an offence against this section, it is not\nnecessary to prove that the person receiving the threat actually\nfeared that the threat would be carried out.\nDefinitions",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-40"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-40-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-40-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8f326378c71e0ec6ffced1599064b65fd8968a5a39de2ff9fa03710a1ba92522",
      "skos:note": "No fear of threat is necessary to prove in prosecution."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-40-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40(3) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "(3) In a prosecution for an offence against this section, it is not\nnecessary to prove that the person receiving the threat actually\nfeared that the threat would be carried out.\nDefinitions"
    },
