      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "(4) For the purposes of subsection (1), an item is taken to be an item of\nchild abuse material if it is a document or other goods:\n\n(a) that depicts a person, or a representation of a person, who:\n\n(i) is, or appears to be, under 18 years of age; and\n\n(ii) is, or appears to be, a victim of torture, cruelty or\nphysical abuse;\n\nand does this in a way that reasonable persons would regard\nas being, in all the circumstances, offensive; or\n\n(b) that describes a person who:\n\n(i) is, or is implied to be, under 18 years of age; and\n\n(ii) is, or is implied to be, a victim of torture, cruelty or\nphysical abuse;\n\nand does this in a way that reasonable persons would regard\nas being, in all the circumstances, offensive.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) For the purposes of subsection (1), an item is taken to be an item of\nchild abuse material if it is a document or other goods:\n\n(a) that depicts a person, or a representation of a person, who:\n\n(i) is, or appears to be, under 18 years of age; and\n\n(ii) is, or appears to be, a victim of torture, cruelty or\nphysical abuse;\n\nand does this in a way that reasonable persons would regard\nas being, in all the circumstances, offensive; or\n\n(b) that describes a person who:\n\n(i) is, or is implied to be, under 18 years of age; and\n\n(ii) is, or is implied to be, a victim of torture, cruelty or\nphysical abuse;\n\nand does this in a way that reasonable persons would regard\nas being, in all the circumstances, offensive.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-44"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-44-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-44-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8b3666d5e0667c31d1074e691be0a4398cc2556bec9e9dfa639aab032513219f",
      "skos:note": "Prohibits the creation, distribution, or possession of child abuse material."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-44-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44(4) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(4) For the purposes of subsection (1), an item is taken to be an item of\nchild abuse material if it is a document or other goods:\n\n(a) that depicts a person, or a representation of a person, who:\n\n(i) is, or appears to be, under 18 years of age; and\n\n(ii) is, or appears to be, a victim of torture, cruelty or\nphysical abuse;\n\nand does this in a way that reasonable persons would regard\nas being, in all the circumstances, offensive; or\n\n(b) that describes a person who:\n\n(i) is, or is implied to be, under 18 years of age; and\n\n(ii) is, or is implied to be, a victim of torture, cruelty or\nphysical abuse;\n\nand does this in a way that reasonable persons would regard\nas being, in all the circumstances, offensive."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-44-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
