      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-44-ss-4a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44(4A) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-44-ss-4a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "(4A) The matters to be taken into account in deciding for the purposes of\nsubsections (3) and (4) whether reasonable persons would regard a\nparticular document or other goods as being, in all the\ncircumstances, offensive, include:\n\n(a) the standards of morality, decency and propriety generally\naccepted by reasonable adults; and\n\n(b) the literary, artistic or educational merit (if any) of the\nmaterial; and\n\n(c) the general character of the material (including whether it is\nof a medical, legal or scientific character).\nTelecommunications (Interception) Act 1979",
      "skos:definition": "(4A) The matters to be taken into account in deciding for the purposes of\nsubsections (3) and (4) whether reasonable persons would regard a\nparticular document or other goods as being, in all the\ncircumstances, offensive, include:\n\n(a) the standards of morality, decency and propriety generally\naccepted by reasonable adults; and\n\n(b) the literary, artistic or educational merit (if any) of the\nmaterial; and\n\n(c) the general character of the material (including whether it is\nof a medical, legal or scientific character).\nTelecommunications (Interception) Act 1979",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-44"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-44-ss-4a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-44-ss-4a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-44-ss-4a-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-44-ss-4a-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-44-ss-4a-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-1-sec-44-ss-4a-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1f378b24be8012804dd094c75713aaef7e9a51f7e1451718d26a22378a36a46c",
      "skos:note": "Consider standards of morality, decency and propriety when evaluating offensive material."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-1-sec-44-ss-4a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44(4A) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(4A) The matters to be taken into account in deciding for the purposes of\nsubsections (3) and (4) whether reasonable persons would regard a\nparticular document or other goods as being, in all the\ncircumstances, offensive, include:\n\n(a) the standards of morality, decency and propriety generally\naccepted by reasonable adults; and\n\n(b) the literary, artistic or educational merit (if any) of the\nmaterial; and\n\n(c) the general character of the material (including whether it is\nof a medical, legal or scientific character).\nTelecommunications (Interception) Act 1979"
    },
