    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-2-sec-380",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "380 1  Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-2-sec-380"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.53",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Part:\nconstitutional trade and commerce means trade and commerce:\n\n(a) with other countries; or\n\n(b) among the States; or\n\n(c) between a State and a Territory; or\n\n(d) between 2 Territories.\ncontaminate goods includes:\n\n(a) interfere with the goods; or\n\n(b) make it appear that the goods have been contaminated or\ninterfered with.\ngoods includes any substance:\n\n(a) whether or not for human consumption; and\n\n(b) whether natural or manufactured; and\n\n(c) whether or not incorporated or mixed with other goods.\n\n(2) A reference in this Part to economic loss caused through public\nawareness of the contamination of goods includes a reference to\neconomic loss caused through:\n\n(a) members of the public not purchasing or using those goods or\nsimilar things; or\n\n(b) steps taken to avoid public alarm or anxiety or to avoid harm\nto members of the public.\n\nContamination offence  Schedule 2",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this Part:\nconstitutional trade and commerce means trade and commerce:\n\n(a) with other countries; or\n\n(b) among the States; or\n\n(c) between a State and a Territory; or\n\n(d) between 2 Territories.\ncontaminate goods includes:\n\n(a) interfere with the goods; or\n\n(b) make it appear that the goods have been contaminated or\ninterfered with.\ngoods includes any substance:\n\n(a) whether or not for human consumption; and\n\n(b) whether natural or manufactured; and\n\n(c) whether or not incorporated or mixed with other goods.\n\n(2) A reference in this Part to economic loss caused through public\nawareness of the contamination of goods includes a reference to\neconomic loss caused through:\n\n(a) members of the public not purchasing or using those goods or\nsimilar things; or\n\n(b) steps taken to avoid public alarm or anxiety or to avoid harm\nto members of the public.\n\nContamination offence  Schedule 2",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-2-sec-380-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-2-sec-380-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d938a99cce92b996887b834319ed0385a5bd0ada85aa7d38eac494fa031f9ecc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-2-sec-380",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "380 1  Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 53,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Part:\nconstitutional trade and commerce means trade and commerce:\n\n(a) with other countries; or\n\n(b) among the States; or\n\n(c) between a State and a Territory; or\n\n(d) between 2 Territories.\ncontaminate goods includes:\n\n(a) interfere with the goods; or\n\n(b) make it appear that the goods have been contaminated or\ninterfered with.\ngoods includes any substance:\n\n(a) whether or not for human consumption; and\n\n(b) whether natural or manufactured; and\n\n(c) whether or not incorporated or mixed with other goods.\n\n(2) A reference in this Part to economic loss caused through public\nawareness of the contamination of goods includes a reference to\neconomic loss caused through:\n\n(a) members of the public not purchasing or using those goods or\nsimilar things; or\n\n(b) steps taken to avoid public alarm or anxiety or to avoid harm\nto members of the public.\n\nContamination offence  Schedule 2"
    },
