      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "Offence based on implied nationhood power\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person makes a threat that goods will be contaminated;\nand\n\n(b) the person does so with intent:\n\n(i) to cause public alarm or anxiety in Australia; or\n\n(ii) to cause widespread, or nationally significant, economic\nloss in Australia through public awareness of the\ncontamination, or possible contamination, of the goods;\nor\n\nContamination offence  Schedule 2",
      "skos:definition": "Offence based on implied nationhood power\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person makes a threat that goods will be contaminated;\nand\n\n(b) the person does so with intent:\n\n(i) to cause public alarm or anxiety in Australia; or\n\n(ii) to cause widespread, or nationally significant, economic\nloss in Australia through public awareness of the\ncontamination, or possible contamination, of the goods;\nor\n\nContamination offence  Schedule 2",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-2-sec-380-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-2-sec-380-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d7b542922a0fa65e5d06411474a4f8c7c7f5272fb5d7b25f032d9c0bab48a482",
      "skos:note": "Threatening to contaminate goods is an offence."
    },
