    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-3-sec-480-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "480 5  Possession or control of thing with intent to dishonestly obtain",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-3-sec-480-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "or deal in personal financial information\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has possession or control of any thing; and\n\n(b) the person has that possession or control with the intention\nthat the thing be used:\n\n(i) by the person; or\n\n(ii) by another person;\n\nto commit an offence against section 480.4 (dishonestly\nobtaining or dealing in personal financial information) or to\nfacilitate the commission of that offence.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 3 years.\n\n(2) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)\neven if committing the offence against section 480.4 (dishonestly\nobtaining or dealing in personal financial information) is\nimpossible.\n\n(3) It is not an offence to attempt to commit an offence against\nsubsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "or deal in personal financial information\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has possession or control of any thing; and\n\n(b) the person has that possession or control with the intention\nthat the thing be used:\n\n(i) by the person; or\n\n(ii) by another person;\n\nto commit an offence against section 480.4 (dishonestly\nobtaining or dealing in personal financial information) or to\nfacilitate the commission of that offence.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 3 years.\n\n(2) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)\neven if committing the offence against section 480.4 (dishonestly\nobtaining or dealing in personal financial information) is\nimpossible.\n\n(3) It is not an offence to attempt to commit an offence against\nsubsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-3-sec-480-5-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-3-sec-480-5-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-3-sec-480-5-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6d5443f1c24f5d075f1e342109f3edd31c67a61ec52bbb99a15764c971bcded8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-3-sec-480-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "480 5  Possession or control of thing with intent to dishonestly obtain",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "or deal in personal financial information\n\n(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has possession or control of any thing; and\n\n(b) the person has that possession or control with the intention\nthat the thing be used:\n\n(i) by the person; or\n\n(ii) by another person;\n\nto commit an offence against section 480.4 (dishonestly\nobtaining or dealing in personal financial information) or to\nfacilitate the commission of that offence.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 3 years.\n\n(2) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)\neven if committing the offence against section 480.4 (dishonestly\nobtaining or dealing in personal financial information) is\nimpossible.\n\n(3) It is not an offence to attempt to commit an offence against\nsubsection (1)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-3-sec-480-5-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "480(1) 5  Possession or control of thing with intent to dishonestly obtain",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-3-sec-480-5-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has possession or control of any thing; and\n\n(b) the person has that possession or control with the intention\nthat the thing be used:\n\n(i) by the person; or\n\n(ii) by another person;\n\nto commit an offence against section 480.4 (dishonestly\nobtaining or dealing in personal financial information) or to\nfacilitate the commission of that offence.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 3 years.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has possession or control of any thing; and\n\n(b) the person has that possession or control with the intention\nthat the thing be used:\n\n(i) by the person; or\n\n(ii) by another person;\n\nto commit an offence against section 480.4 (dishonestly\nobtaining or dealing in personal financial information) or to\nfacilitate the commission of that offence.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 3 years.",
