    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-4-sec-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 Transitional—pre-commencement offences",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-4-sec-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.65",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nDespite the amendment or repeal of a provision by this Part, that\nprovision continues to apply, after the commencement of this item, in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) an offence committed before the commencement of this item;\nor\n\n(b) proceedings for an offence alleged to have been committed\nbefore the commencement of this item; or\n\n(c) any matter connected with, or arising out of, such\nproceedings;\nas if the amendment or repeal had not been made.\n(2)\nSubitem (1) does not limit the operation of section 8 of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\nAmendment of other Acts  Schedule 5",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nDespite the amendment or repeal of a provision by this Part, that\nprovision continues to apply, after the commencement of this item, in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) an offence committed before the commencement of this item;\nor\n\n(b) proceedings for an offence alleged to have been committed\nbefore the commencement of this item; or\n\n(c) any matter connected with, or arising out of, such\nproceedings;\nas if the amendment or repeal had not been made.\n(2)\nSubitem (1) does not limit the operation of section 8 of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\nAmendment of other Acts  Schedule 5",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-4-sec-8-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dfc899a6086bfadc79d307ab76925af35b854569d1fd2fcf3a2a75bbb0d5f8f4",
      "skos:note": "Continues to apply provisions before commencement of item."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-4-sec-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 Transitional—pre-commencement offences",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 65,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nDespite the amendment or repeal of a provision by this Part, that\nprovision continues to apply, after the commencement of this item, in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) an offence committed before the commencement of this item;\nor\n\n(b) proceedings for an offence alleged to have been committed\nbefore the commencement of this item; or\n\n(c) any matter connected with, or arising out of, such\nproceedings;\nas if the amendment or repeal had not been made.\n(2)\nSubitem (1) does not limit the operation of section 8 of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\nAmendment of other Acts  Schedule 5"
    },
    {
