    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-5-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Subsection 233B(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-5-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) possesses goods on board a ship or aircraft; or\n\n(ii) brings goods into Australia; or\n\n(iii) imports goods into Australia; or\n\n(iv) possesses goods that have been imported into Australia\nin contravention of this Act; or\n\n(v) conveys goods that have been imported into Australia in\ncontravention of this Act; or\n\n(vi) possesses goods that are reasonably suspected of having\nbeen imported into Australia in contravention of this\nAct; or\n\nAmendment of other Acts  Schedule 5\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    61\n\n(vii) fails to disclose to an officer on demand any knowledge\nin his or her possession or power concerning the\nimportation or intended importation, or bringing or\nintended bringing, into Australia of goods; and\n\n(b) the goods are a prohibited import to which this section\napplies.\n\n(1AAB) Subparagraph (1)(a)(i), (ii), (iv), (v) or (vi) does not apply if the\nperson proves that the person had a reasonable excuse for doing the\nact referred to in that subparagraph.\n\n(1AAC) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) exports goods from Australia; or\n\n(ii) fails to disclose to an officer on demand any knowledge\nin his or her possession or power concerning the\nexportation or intended exportation from Australia of\ngoods; and\n\n(b) the goods are a prohibited export to which this section\napplies.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) possesses goods on board a ship or aircraft; or\n\n(ii) brings goods into Australia; or\n\n(iii) imports goods into Australia; or\n\n(iv) possesses goods that have been imported into Australia\nin contravention of this Act; or\n\n(v) conveys goods that have been imported into Australia in\ncontravention of this Act; or\n\n(vi) possesses goods that are reasonably suspected of having\nbeen imported into Australia in contravention of this\nAct; or\n\nAmendment of other Acts  Schedule 5\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    61\n\n(vii) fails to disclose to an officer on demand any knowledge\nin his or her possession or power concerning the\nimportation or intended importation, or bringing or\nintended bringing, into Australia of goods; and\n\n(b) the goods are a prohibited import to which this section\napplies.\n\n(1AAB) Subparagraph (1)(a)(i), (ii), (iv), (v) or (vi) does not apply if the\nperson proves that the person had a reasonable excuse for doing the\nact referred to in that subparagraph.\n\n(1AAC) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) exports goods from Australia; or\n\n(ii) fails to disclose to an officer on demand any knowledge\nin his or her possession or power concerning the\nexportation or intended exportation from Australia of\ngoods; and\n\n(b) the goods are a prohibited export to which this section\napplies.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-5-sec-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-5-sec-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-5-sec-3-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:act-sch-5-sec-3-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b4defcc814773d03b5de2ad0e74beea411670d40ab09452234c78b654df041de",
      "skos:note": "Possessing or bringing prohibited goods into Australia is an offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/act#sch-5-sec-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Subsection 233B(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) possesses goods on board a ship or aircraft; or\n\n(ii) brings goods into Australia; or\n\n(iii) imports goods into Australia; or\n\n(iv) possesses goods that have been imported into Australia\nin contravention of this Act; or\n\n(v) conveys goods that have been imported into Australia in\ncontravention of this Act; or\n\n(vi) possesses goods that are reasonably suspected of having\nbeen imported into Australia in contravention of this\nAct; or\n\nAmendment of other Acts  Schedule 5\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    61\n\n(vii) fails to disclose to an officer on demand any knowledge\nin his or her possession or power concerning the\nimportation or intended importation, or bringing or\nintended bringing, into Australia of goods; and\n\n(b) the goods are a prohibited import to which this section\napplies.\n\n(1AAB) Subparagraph (1)(a)(i), (ii), (iv), (v) or (vi) does not apply if the\nperson proves that the person had a reasonable excuse for doing the\nact referred to in that subparagraph.\n\n(1AAC) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) exports goods from Australia; or\n\n(ii) fails to disclose to an officer on demand any knowledge\nin his or her possession or power concerning the\nexportation or intended exportation from Australia of\ngoods; and\n\n(b) the goods are a prohibited export to which this section\napplies."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-5-sec-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:act-sch-5-sec-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-5-sec-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits possessing or bringing prohibited goods into Australia.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person possesses goods on board a ship or aircraft; or brings goods into Australia; or imports goods into Australia; or possesses goods that have been imported into Australia in contravention of this Act;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "An offence is committed if the person possesses or brings prohibited goods into Australia."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-5-sec-3-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits exporting prohibited goods from Australia.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) The person exports goods from Australia; or fails to disclose to an officer on demand any knowledge in his or her possession or power concerning the exportation or intended exportation from Australia of goods;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "An offence is committed if the person exports prohibited goods from Australia."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-5-sec-3-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Justify",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Justifies the prohibition on possessing or bringing prohibited goods into Australia.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1AAB) Subparagraph (1)(a)(i), (ii), (iv), (v) or (vi) does not apply if the person proves that the person had a reasonable excuse for doing the act referred to in that subparagraph.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person may justify their action if they have a reasonable excuse."
    },
